         ${misc:Depends}
Description: Aurora boot splash
 aura, the bootloader, draws the Aurora logo centred on a black screen and
 U-Boot leaves it there. This Plymouth theme draws the same image at the same
 size and place on every panel, so the logo stays still from power-on until
 the login screen. The spinner sits below it and the distribution's branding
 (the spinner theme's watermark) at the bottom. Disk passwords are asked on
 the same screen; Esc shows the boot messages.
 .
 Before plymouthd starts, /usr/libexec/aurora-plymouth reads the boot panel's
 geometry from the live device tree; a dracut module runs it in the initramfs.
